  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.5.0: navigation gained parameters and cache control — FluentFrame.Navigate(pageType, parameter) and the generic overloads key both the cache and the history by type plus parameter, so one page type reached with different arguments keeps separate instances; new CacheSize (10 by default), PageFactory (Func<Type, object, Control>), CurrentPageType, CurrentParameter and CurrentCacheMode; FluentPage.NavigationCacheMode takes Disabled, Enabled or Required and pages override OnNavigatedTo / OnNavigatedFrom to read NavigationEventArgs, while any other control opts in through INavigationAware. NavigationViewItemHeader and NavigationViewItemSeparator can be mixed into MenuItems and FooterMenuItems, are never selectable and take no space in the compact pane, and NavigationViewItem.Tag is now the navigation parameter. New FluentTaskbarProgress component with TaskbarProgressState (None, Indeterminate, Normal, Error, Paused, matching the shell TBPFLAG values) paints determinate, indeterminate, paused and error progress on a form’s taskbar button, marshalling shell calls onto the form’s UI thread and degrading silently where the interface is absent. Fixed FluentPage keeping the previous theme’s blended surface after a switch to the dark theme — the page recomputed its background before its window applied the new one, so a dark page came out washed out; the recalculation is now deferred until the notification round has finished. 1.4.2: packaging metadata only, no code change — the package now declares PackageProjectUrl plus the git repository location, so the nuget.org page links back to the GitHub source. 1.4.1: two fixes from live testing on .NET Framework 4.6. FluentDataGridView scrollbars no longer leave a stale Fluent thumb in the channel when the mouse wheel scrolls the grid body — a native scrollbar child window moves its thumb by blitting inside SetScrollInfo and never sends WM_PAINT to the subclassed window procedure (RedrawWindow with RDW_UPDATENOW does not deliver one either), so repaints now go through InvalidateRect plus UpdateWindow and also run after the Scroll event. FluentRichTextBox no longer throws System.OverflowException in a 64-bit process after IsTextSelectionEnabled is turned off: the selection gate read WParam.ToInt32() for every message and messages that carry a pointer in wParam (WM_MOUSEACTIVATE with a parent HWND, WM_CTLCOLOR* with an HDC) exceed the Int32 range, so it now masks the low word with WParam.ToInt64() and 0xFFFF. 1.4.0: major control catalog expansion — added FluentIcon (symbol/glyph/image presenter), FluentPictureBox (rounded-corner picture box), FluentToolStrip (themed tool strip), FluentRichTextBox (Fluent rich-text shell with read-only selectable mode), FluentScrollBar (slim auto-hiding scroll bar), FluentCodeBlock (syntax-highlighted, copyable code presenter), FluentTabView (browser-style tab container with reorder and cancelable add/close), FluentNotifyIcon (system tray component), FluentToast (in-app floating notifications), FluentWrapPanel / FluentUniformGrid layout panels, FluentGridView (virtualized tile view with data binding), FluentTreeGrid (multi-column tree list) and FluentTitleBar (custom title bar for borderless forms: drag, double-click maximize, edge resize, system menu); Gallery gained Widgets and Layouts pages; toolbox manifest and Chinese reference docs updated. 1.3.0: added FluentMaskedTextBox, FluentCheckedListBox, FluentErrorProvider, FluentStatusStrip and FluentSplitContainer — native mask validation and editing, per-item check states with data binding, validation borders/icons/tooltips, the native StatusStrip item model, and native split panels with a themed splitter and native non-docked default; all five support light/dark themes and Visual Studio toolbox/designer integration. 1.2.4: fixed the black client area after restoring a minimized window on Windows 11 — DWM discards the redirection surface of backdrop-class windows while minimized and restore does not repaint it automatically; FluentWindow now invalidates itself and its children when restored from minimize. 1.2.3: fixed the DWM system-backdrop enum being off by one against the Windows SDK — \"None\" silently enabled AUTO (Mica), which could corrupt the window (black client area, stale theme colors) after minimize/restore; Mica/Acrylic/Tabbed now select the correct backdrop types. 1.2.2: fixed white boxes and invisible text after switching to the dark theme — FluentWindow now syncs its BackColor with the theme palette so ambiently-inheriting child controls repaint on the dark surface. 1.2.1: FluentWindow now defaults to a solid Fluent background — the full-client Mica glass pass double-composites GDI-rendered pixels and ghosted text on Windows 11; Mica/Acrylic remain opt-in via BackdropType. 1.2.0: .NET Framework support lowered to 4.6+ — the net48 target is replaced by net46 (one assembly compatible with 4.6 through 4.8); DPI queries fall back to the OS on frameworks without Control.DeviceDpi. 1.1.7: drop-down list no longer hides the items above the selection after picking an item. 1.1.6: \"Edit Items...\" smart tag link opens the string collection editor in the .NET 6/8/10 out-of-process designer. 1.1.5: native ComboBox-style smart tag — \"Use Data Bound Items\" checkbox, unbound \"Edit Items...\" string collection editor, bound data-source drop-down and member fields. 1.1.4: real data-source drop-down + localized smart tag labels. 1.1.3: smart tag in the .NET 6/8/10 out-of-process designer. 1.1.1: ListControl-style data binding. 1.1.0: Chinese manual; categorized toolbox.",
